{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MaximalCliques","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques","role":"collection","title":"Cliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/shuffled()":{"abstract":[],"title":"shuffled()","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"shuffled","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/shuffled()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/shuffled()","kind":"symbol"}}}